conflictcounts.tex.caption:
Director rewrite counts among known films ($n/N$). Exact-name targets count edits
  matching a real-world director credit. Surrogate controls count any Director change;
  none matches the paired film's real credit.

decoding.tex.caption:
Hospital S repairs by recovery category. Unique and Ambig. use the 24-syllable inventory;
  Generic covers English terms, and Digits covers numeric tokens. Headers give cell counts, covering
  217 of 219 errors, with two address-spacing errors excluded from these counts.

movieserrors.tex.caption:
Movies' 1,965 errors and their transfer mechanisms. Source-style errors occupy
  190 rows, with formatting rules also applied table-wide. Copied errors transfer cell recipes;
  drawn errors follow measured rates. Slugs are the film identifiers used in Rotten Tomatoes URLs.

rayyan.tex.caption:
Rayyan's stratified field checks. $N_h$: error population; $n_h$: sampled;
  $m_h$: title-matched; $b_h$: failed reference checks; $d_h$: passed dirty checks.
  A dash denotes an unassessed dirty-side check.
